# Expectation record for 14_abi_calling_convention/004_small_and_large_struct_passing.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 004_small_and_large_struct_passing
area               = 14_abi_calling_convention
description        = Aggregates passed by value on both sides of every target's by-register versus by-memory threshold: an 8-byte struct passed ten times over, four different 16-byte layouts (all-int, mixed, all-double, all-float) passed five times each, a 24-byte struct and a 40-byte struct, in a folded and a volatile-runtime variant
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Free of undefined and unspecified behaviour by construction:
- Every floating value is a dyadic rational exactly representable in binary32 and binary64
  alike, printed with an explicit precision with room to spare, so no rounding decision is
  taken and i686's x87 extended intermediate precision cannot perturb a result. Each float
  member is cast to double explicitly where it is printed. No non-finite value, no negative
  zero and no division appears.
- No signed integer overflow; every integer member is within +/-9210 and none is
  arithmetically combined.
- No shift operator appears, so no shift count can be out of range.
- PADDING DISCIPLINE, which is the central hazard for this program. sizeof is never printed
  and no aggregate is ever memcmp'd or inspected byte-wise. Only NAMED MEMBERS are read
  back, so the fact that the mixed int-and-double aggregate is 12 bytes on i686 (where
  double has four-byte alignment) and 16 bytes on the other three targets cannot affect the
  output, and no padding byte is ever read.
- Array members are indexed only with constant indices strictly inside their bounds, so no
  one-past-end pointer is formed and none is dereferenced.
- No aliasing violation: every aggregate is copied whole by assignment between objects of
  the same type, never through a converted pointer.
- No read of uninitialized storage: every static aggregate has an initializer and every
  staged local is assigned from its volatile counterpart before it is passed.
- No object is modified twice between sequence points.
- NOTHING DEPENDS ON UNSPECIFIED EVALUATION ORDER, and this is enforced structurally
  rather than argued. An access to a volatile object IS an observable side effect and the
  order in which a call's arguments are evaluated is unspecified, so every volatile datum
  is read exactly once, in a statement of its own, and only the resulting plain locals are
  passed. Machine-checked on this branch: flattening the program into statements and
  counting references to its volatile objects finds NO statement with more than one. The
  snapshots cost nothing in coverage, because each is itself a load from volatile storage
  that the optimizer may neither fold nor elide, so every value the callee receives was
  genuinely materialised at run time and marshalled through the ABI; what changed is only
  that the loads are now SEQUENCED rather than unordered.
- Hermetic, as constraint C4 requires: every input is a literal in the source. Nothing is
  opened, no socket is created, no environment variable and no program argument is read,
  and no storage is obtained from the heap.
- main returns 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires.
- Verified empirically on this branch: the default strict warning gate
  (-Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror) produces zero
  diagnostics at -O0, -O1 and -O2, and -fsanitize=undefined,address
  -fno-sanitize-recover=all runs to completion with empty stderr and exit status 0.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
WHICH REGISTER FILE EACH SHAPE ACTUALLY EXHAUSTS, stated per function rather than as one
blanket claim, because the shapes do not behave alike and a single sentence about
"exhausting the register files" would be false for two of them. Every reading below was
MEASURED in the reference compiler's -O0 assembly for each target with a purpose-built
probe. Slot counts are for the aggregates only; the trailing int tag is counted separately.
System V i386 cdecl marshals every argument of every one of these calls on the stack, so it
is not repeated per row.

  take_s8x10   10 x 8-byte two-int aggregate. One integer slot each on all three 64-bit
               ABIs, so 10 plus the tag = 11: EXHAUSTS the integer file on all three (6 on
               AMD64, 8 on AAPCS64, 8 on LP64D) and spills. No floating slot used.
  take_s16ix5   5 x 16-byte four-int aggregate. Two integer slots each = 10 plus the tag:
               EXHAUSTS the integer file on all three and spills. No floating slot used.
  take_s16mx5   5 x mixed int-and-double. The shape that makes a blanket claim wrong. AMD64
               classifies each INTEGER + SSE, so 5 integer slots plus the tag fills EXACTLY
               the six integer registers while using only 5 of 8 SSE -- the floating file is
               NOT exhausted. AAPCS64 sees a non-homogeneous 16-byte aggregate and uses two
               integer slots each = 10 plus the tag, exhausting x0-x7 and using no floating
               ARGUMENT register at all. LP64D splits each into one integer plus one
               floating slot, so 6 of 8 integer with the tag and 5 of 8 floating: NEITHER
               file is exhausted there, and what the call exercises is the independent
               advance of the two allocators.
  take_s16dx5   5 x two-double aggregate. Two floating slots each = 10, so the FLOATING file
               is exhausted on all three. The overflow differs, and that difference is part
               of the point: AMD64 and AAPCS64 stack the fifth aggregate and use one integer
               register for the tag, whereas LP64D spills the two remaining doubles into
               INTEGER argument registers before the tag, so there the integer file carries
               floating data as well.
  take_s16fx5   5 x four-float aggregate. AMD64 packs each into two SSE registers = 10, so
               the floating file is exhausted. AAPCS64 treats each as a four-float
               homogeneous aggregate = 20 floating slots, exhausted far past the threshold.
               LP64D declines the floating path for a 16-byte four-member aggregate and uses
               two integer slots each = 10 plus the tag, so there it is the INTEGER file
               that is exhausted. The same source shape exhausts different files on
               different targets, which is exactly the disagreement worth testing.
  take_s24x4    4 x 24-byte aggregate. Memory on every target -- AMD64 by the MEMORY class,
               AAPCS64 and LP64D by an indirect reference -- so no file is exhausted; the
               by-memory path itself is the subject.
  take_sbigx2   2 x 40-byte aggregate. Unambiguously memory everywhere, for the same reason.

COVERAGE OF THE BY-MEMORY SHAPES. For the 40-byte aggregate every one of the ten members is
read back rather than a sample of three, because a copy that corrupted only an interior
member would otherwise leave no trace in stdout and the by-memory path would be exercised
without being observed.

THE CALL BARRIER. Every call this program makes to the function whose ABI boundary is
under test goes through a FILE-SCOPE volatile FUNCTION POINTER, and that is load-bearing
rather than stylistic. A C11 volatile lvalue must be re-read on every access, so no
conforming compiler may assume which function the pointer designates: it can neither
inline the callee nor clone it, and it must marshal the arguments exactly as the ABI
prescribes because it cannot know what will receive them. This is plain standard C rather
than a compiler attribute, so both sides of oracle (a) honour it for the same reason and
neither needs to support an extension for the barrier to hold. It also makes the
function-pointer load the ONLY volatile access in each call expression, which is what
keeps the one-side-effecting-argument rule satisfied. Measured before-state on this branch: with direct calls, gcc 13.4.0 at
-O2 left only take_s8x10 standing -- the other six were inlined away, so six of the seven
documented boundaries were not crossed at that level. Measured after: all seven callees are
emitted unmodified at -O1 and -O2 on all four targets, with no .constprop and no .isra
clone anywhere.

Plain char signedness is implementation-defined and was measured as signed on x86_64 and
i686 and unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64; no plain-char value is printed. sizeof(long) and
sizeof(void *) were measured as 4 on i686 and 8 on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64
(docs/technical-specifications.md lines 457-462); no long, size_t, ptrdiff_t, intptr_t or
pointer value is printed and no long or pointer conversion specification is used. long
double has three different representations across the four targets (measured 16, 12, 16 and
16 bytes; x87 80-bit versus IEEE binary128) and is absent from this program entirely --
using it would import a difference that has nothing to do with parameter passing. That
type is covered by 13_floating_point/004_long_double_target_restricted, whose record
disables oracle (b) alone with the measured reason recorded and carries NO marker.

No target is dropped, no oracle is disabled and this record carries no expected-divergence
marker: a cross-backend divergence here is a GENUINE FINDING rather than an
implementation-defined difference, because nothing implementation-defined reaches the
output. Measured on this branch with gcc 13.4.0 and the matching i686, aarch64 and riscv64
cross drivers, executed natively and under QEMU user-mode 10.1.0: stdout is byte-identical
and the exit status is 0 in all twelve target-and-optimization-level cells.
END
